menu "CSI Presence Sensor"

    config CSI_WIFI_SSID
        string "Home WiFi SSID"
        default "myssid"
        help
            The router this node associates with. CSI is measured on the link
            to this AP, so put the node where you want to sense.

    config CSI_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Home WiFi password"
        default "mypassword"

    config CSI_LOCATION
        string "Room name"
        default "living room"
        help
            Shown on the dashboard card.

    config CSI_HOST_IP
        string "Host IP running the bridge"
        default "192.168.1.100"
        help
            Telemetry JSON is sent here over UDP. Set this to the LAN IP of the
            computer running bridge/bridge.py.

    config CSI_TELEMETRY_PORT
        int "Telemetry UDP port (to host)"
        default 5566

    config CSI_COMMAND_PORT
        int "Command UDP port (from host)"
        default 5567
        help
            The node listens here for the "CAL" command sent by the dashboard's
            Calibrate button.

    config CSI_PACKET_RATE
        int "Traffic generator rate (packets/second)"
        default 100
        range 10 500
        help
            UDP packets sent to the gateway per second. The router's ACKs are
            what actually produce CSI, so this sets the CSI sample rate. 100 is
            a good default; lower it if your router rate-limits or the link is
            congested.

endmenu
